1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,920
You miss the last step of the subway

2
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:02,360
stairs.

3
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:05,220
You're falling backwards into a crowd of strangers.

4
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:10,020
And then your arm stretches four metres across

5
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:13,400
the station, wraps around a railing, and pulls

6
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:14,500
you back like a bungee cord.

7
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:16,500
Nobody saw it.

8
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:18,320
Everybody was looking at their phone.

9
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:20,280
You look at your hand.

10
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:21,880
It's normal again.

11
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:24,520
Your heart is beating like a drum.

12
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:25,260
Boom.

13
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:26,260
Boom.

14
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:27,340
Boom.

15
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:30,800
Overnight, you got the powers of Monkey D.

16
00:00:31,060 --> 00:00:32,000
Luffy from One Piece.

17
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:33,520
Not his straw hat.

18
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:34,480
Not his crew.

19
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:36,100
Just his body.

20
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:38,420
A body made of rubber.

21
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:39,800
Four gears.

22
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:43,540
And one last form, Gear 5, so powerful

23
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:45,400
that it leaves Luffy looking like an old

24
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:46,220
man when it ends.

25
00:00:47,160 --> 00:00:49,660
In the next sixty days you'll learn what

26
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:52,940
rubber can really do, what it can't, and

27
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:55,240
why the strongest thing you have also costs

28
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:55,840
the most.

29
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:58,320
First test: the mirror.

30
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:00,600
You pinch your cheek and pull.

31
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,840
It stretches thirty centimetres and snaps back.

32
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:07,100
Real rubber is stretchy, but it has limits.

33
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:10,180
Natural rubber usually breaks when it's stretched to

34
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:12,460
somewhere between four and ten times its length.

35
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:15,040
Luffy goes far beyond that.

36
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:18,280
Your arm just did four metres without tearing.

37
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:20,520
Then you notice something weird.

38
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:23,220
When you stretch, your arm gets warm.

39
00:01:23,860 --> 00:01:25,560
When it snaps back, it goes cold.

40
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:27,060
That one's real.

41
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:29,140
It's called the Gough-Joule effect.

42
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:31,660
Stretch a rubber band fast and touch it

43
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:33,160
to your lips, and you'll feel it warm

44
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:33,520
up.

45
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:36,680
Stretching lines up the long molecules inside the

46
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:38,020
rubber, and that releases heat.

47
00:01:38,820 --> 00:01:39,760
Letting go does the opposite.

48
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:43,340
So rule one: every stretch makes you warm.

49
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:45,480
A hundred stretches, and you're sweating.

50
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:48,680
Luffy's most famous move is simple.

51
00:01:49,340 --> 00:01:51,480
Stretch your arm back, let go, and it

52
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:52,880
flies forward like a slingshot.

53
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:54,540
You try it on a punching bag.

54
00:01:55,020 --> 00:01:57,420
You pull your arm back ten metres.

55
00:01:57,420 --> 00:01:57,900
You let go.

56
00:01:58,420 --> 00:02:00,720
The bag rips off its chain and lands

57
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:01,700
on the other side of the court.

58
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:04,880
A slingshot stores energy while you stretch it,

59
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:06,460
and gives it all back at once.

60
00:02:06,940 --> 00:02:08,520
The further you pull, the more energy.

61
00:02:09,260 --> 00:02:11,400
But there's a catch Luffy never mentions.

62
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:14,080
Your arm also has to come back.

63
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:16,200
And it comes back just as fast.

64
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:18,540
You punch yourself in the face with your

65
00:02:18,540 --> 00:02:19,180
own elbow.

66
00:02:19,780 --> 00:02:20,000
Twice.

67
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,360
Rule two: what you throw, comes back.

68
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:26,700
In One Piece, Luffy beats a man made

69
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:29,440
of lightning, because his rubber body doesn't conduct

70
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:29,880
electricity.

71
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:32,900
So on day six, when a thunderstorm rolls

72
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:34,600
in, you climb to the roof to find

73
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:36,160
out if that's true for you too.

74
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:38,880
Ordinary rubber would lose this fight.

75
00:02:39,460 --> 00:02:41,800
A typical lightning bolt carries about three hundred

76
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:42,660
million volts.

77
00:02:43,220 --> 00:02:45,300
The thick rubber gloves electricians wear on power

78
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:48,060
lines are rated for thirty-six thousand.

79
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:50,420
Lightning is more than eight thousand times that.

80
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:53,320
Push enough voltage through any insulator and it

81
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:54,800
suddenly gives up and conducts.

82
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:57,560
Physicists call it dielectric breakdown.

83
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:00,280
Even car tyres don't protect you from lightning.

84
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:02,180
What protects you in a car is the

85
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:04,340
metal body, which carries the current around you.

86
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:06,960
But you're not ordinary rubber.

87
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:09,660
The bolt hits the lightning rod next door,

88
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:11,960
jumps to you, and nothing happens.

89
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:13,040
No shock.

90
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:13,860
No pain.

91
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,240
Your body is the one thing in this

92
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:17,380
story that follows the manga.

93
00:03:18,220 --> 00:03:20,460
Your phone, though, is not made of Nika

94
00:03:20,460 --> 00:03:20,660
rubber.

95
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:22,600
And the air around a lightning bolt gets

96
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:24,600
about five times hotter than the surface of

97
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:24,920
the Sun.

98
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:26,620
Your hoodie is smoking.

99
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:28,680
Your sneakers have melted to the roof.

100
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:31,100
Rule three: you beat the voltage.

101
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:32,480
You don't beat the heat.

102
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:35,560
You get a job loading trucks at a

103
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:38,280
frozen-food warehouse, because nobody else can carry that

104
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:39,440
many boxes at once.

105
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:42,400
At minus twenty degrees, your arms feel stiff.

106
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:43,340
Slower.

107
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:44,700
Like old elastic.

108
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:47,440
Real rubber has a breaking point in the

109
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:47,700
cold.

110
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:51,200
Below about minus sixty, natural rubber stops being

111
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:53,880
stretchy and turns hard and brittle, like glass.

112
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:56,740
Only a few places on Earth ever get

113
00:03:56,740 --> 00:03:59,380
that cold, deep in Siberia in winter and

114
00:03:59,380 --> 00:03:59,940
in Antarctica.

115
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:02,780
Now you know the two places you'll never

116
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:03,500
take a holiday.

117
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:06,960
A forklift loses its brakes on a ramp

118
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:08,840
and rolls toward a coworker.

119
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:10,660
You do the thing Luffy does when he

120
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:11,340
needs speed.

121
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:12,240
Gear 2.

122
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:14,980
You pump your blood faster, and your skin

123
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:15,900
starts to steam.

124
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:18,220
You move faster than anyone in the warehouse

125
00:04:18,220 --> 00:04:18,800
can see.

126
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,380
The forklift stops against your hands.

127
00:04:22,340 --> 00:04:23,920
Here's what Gear 2 does to a real

128
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:24,300
body.

129
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:27,220
A healthy heart's maximum is roughly two hundred

130
00:04:27,220 --> 00:04:28,680
and twenty minus your age.

131
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:31,360
For a twenty-year-old, around two hundred beats a

132
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:31,660
minute.

133
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:34,460
Gear 2 pushes past that, on purpose.

134
00:04:35,260 --> 00:04:37,340
In the early story, people warned Luffy that

135
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:38,600
it was shortening his life.

136
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:41,220
You sit on a crate afterwards, your heart

137
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:42,260
racing for an hour.

138
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:43,460
Rule four:

139
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:45,120
speed is borrowed.

140
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:46,400
You pay it back.

141
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:48,840
Gear 3.

142
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:50,860
You bite your thumb and blow into it,

143
00:04:50,860 --> 00:04:52,320
and your bones inflate.

144
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:54,820
Your fist becomes the size of a car.

145
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:57,000
A steel beam slips off a crane.

146
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,220
You catch it with a hand as big

147
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:00,100
as a garage door.

148
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:03,520
And then, like early Luffy, your body shrinks

149
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:04,580
back down for a while.

150
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:07,380
You walk home the size of a ten-year-old,

151
00:05:07,380 --> 00:05:09,500
in clothes that are far too big.

152
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:10,500
Rule five:

153
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:12,500
big now, small later.

154
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:14,960
By now there are videos.

155
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:16,340
A forklift.

156
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:17,160
A crane.

157
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:20,040
A kid who suddenly got very small, very

158
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:20,620
fast.

159
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:22,860
Nobody has your name yet.

160
00:05:23,260 --> 00:05:25,740
But two people in suits knock on your

161
00:05:25,740 --> 00:05:28,300
door and ask, very politely, if you'd like

162
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:28,740
a job.

163
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:30,100
You say no.

164
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:31,740
They leave a card.

165
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:33,620
They don't seem surprised.

166
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:36,720
That night you try the strongest form you

167
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:37,120
know:

168
00:05:37,760 --> 00:05:38,040
Gear 4.

169
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:40,400
You blow air into your muscles until they

170
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:42,880
swell like armour, and your arms and legs

171
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:44,180
turn black and hard.

172
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:47,220
In One Piece that black coating is Armament

173
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:50,180
Haki, a willpower that hardens the skin like

174
00:05:50,180 --> 00:05:50,480
steel.

175
00:05:51,440 --> 00:05:53,360
For about a minute, nothing can touch you.

176
00:05:54,340 --> 00:05:56,940
Then it ends, and Luffy's rule hits you

177
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:57,220
too.

178
00:05:58,200 --> 00:05:59,540
No armour.

179
00:05:59,540 --> 00:06:01,420
No Haki.

180
00:06:01,420 --> 00:06:03,340
Ten whole minutes where you're just a tired

181
00:06:03,340 --> 00:06:04,860
person in a parking lot.

182
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:07,680
The next night, you notice a drone.

183
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:10,240
It has been following you since you left

184
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:10,720
the warehouse.

185
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:13,100
The people in suits didn't come back to

186
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:13,420
talk.

187
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
They came back to watch.

188
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:18,040
And now they know exactly how long your

189
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:21,100
strongest form lasts, and exactly how long you're

190
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,000
open afterwards.

191
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,820
Ten minutes is enough for a net,

192
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:27,760
a van, and a very quiet drive.

193
00:06:28,740 --> 00:06:30,540
So you make a new rule, the one

194
00:06:30,540 --> 00:06:32,840
Luffy never needed because he always had his

195
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:33,080
crew:

196
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:35,600
never use Gear 4 alone.

197
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:39,920
Rule six: your strongest minute is also your

198
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:41,740
weakest ten.

199
00:06:41,740 --> 00:06:42,940
Day forty.

200
00:06:42,940 --> 00:06:45,880
A gas main explodes under a busy square.

201
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:47,200
Cars tip over.

202
00:06:47,460 --> 00:06:49,340
A bus is sliding toward the hole.

203
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:51,380
Your heart starts to drum.

204
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:52,180
Boom.

205
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:53,120
Boom.

206
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:54,920
Boom-boom.

207
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:55,400
Gear 5.

208
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:57,280
Your hair turns white.

209
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,760
You laugh, and you don't know why.

210
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,780
And the rules stop applying.

211
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:04,500
You turn the road itself into rubber.

212
00:07:05,060 --> 00:07:06,980
The bus bounces back onto the street like

213
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:07,420
a toy.

214
00:07:08,220 --> 00:07:10,800
You stretch the falling streetlights into soft loops

215
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,160
and lay them down gently.

216
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:15,200
For thirty seconds, the whole city is a

217
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:17,680
cartoon, and you are the only one drawing

218
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:17,980
it.

219
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:20,180
The people in the square don't scream.

220
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:21,120
They stare.

221
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:24,000
One woman laughs with you without knowing why.

222
00:07:24,540 --> 00:07:26,780
A man films everything with his mouth open.

223
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:29,320
And you can't stop laughing.

224
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:31,700
It isn't happiness exactly.

225
00:07:32,180 --> 00:07:35,040
It's the power itself, loud and free, like

226
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:36,440
a song you can't turn off.

227
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:38,880
Somewhere in the back of your head, a

228
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:40,200
quieter voice is counting.

229
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,900
Because every second of this is being paid

230
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:43,140
for.

231
00:07:44,180 --> 00:07:45,600
Then it ends.

232
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:48,720
And the cost of Gear 5 arrives all

233
00:07:48,720 --> 00:07:50,780
at once, just like it does for Luffy.

234
00:07:51,540 --> 00:07:52,960
Your face goes wrinkled.

235
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:54,540
Your legs won't hold you.

236
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:56,940
You look eighty years old, sitting on the

237
00:07:56,940 --> 00:07:58,760
curb, laughing at nothing.

238
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:00,620
It wears off by morning.

239
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:02,160
But now you know:

240
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:05,100
the most powerful thing you can do is

241
00:08:05,100 --> 00:08:07,040
also the thing you can do least.

242
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:10,720
So if you woke up tomorrow made of

243
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:12,900
rubber, which gear would you use first?

244
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:15,120
And which one would you never touch?

245
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:16,680
Tell us in the comments.
